WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.510
Panic had set in.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:03.510
Researchers were frantic.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:09.510
There was a buzz of activity, not born of
excitement but from sheer, widespread fear.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.840
The Scarlet King was coming.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.980
Nobody at the Foundation knew when, or even
how, the monstrous multiversal tyrant would

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.790
spring free and bring endless chaos with him.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.160
But everyone knew it would be soon.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.279
They’d all had the same warning, the same
nightmare.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:29.849
In fact, it wasn’t just the Foundation either;
the entire world had shivered in their sleep,

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:33.989
sharing in the bad dream of the destruction
that was yet to come.

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:37.390
The personnel of the SCP Foundation were on
high alert.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.830
Of course, the organization had been aware
of the impending threat of the Scarlet King

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.280
for longer than almost anyone else.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.270
But that was part of the problem: through
some anomalous dream, had by everyone on Earth,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.199
now everyone else did know.

00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:55.660
The Foundation was less interested in uncovering
the source of the nightmare, and more trying

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.699
to counteract its potential side effects.

00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:03.630
That was what potentially offered the Scarlet
King the power he needed to enter into reality,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:08.670
after all; the more people knew about him,
tried to understand or define the eldritch

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.330
entity, the more power he was able to obtain.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:15.759
“We have an army!” one member of personnel
chimed in during a frantic debate.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:20.020
“We have an almost unlimited fighting force
that are specially trained to handle anomalous

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.470
threats: the Mobile Task Forces!”

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.490
“Are you crazy?”

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.490
another argued.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.100
“The MTFs are certainly not unlimited.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.080
At any rate, the Scarlet King might be one
of the most powerful beings in the entire

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.369
multiverse!

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:36.270
How can our troops, even our anomalous units,
even hope to stand against that?

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.329
You’re proposing sending our own people
into a slaughter!”

00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:42.990
“They’d all be wiped out in a moment,”
one of the other researchers concurred.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.979
“We need to be focusing our efforts on the
amnestic rollout!

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:49.329
If we can distribute enough to the population,
we can wipe their collective memories of the

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:50.590
dream from the other night.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.899
They’ll forget, and that should slow the
approach of the Scarlet King.”

00:01:53.899 --> 00:01:56.520
“Slow him, maybe – but it won’t stop
him!”

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.950
the first retorted.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.549
“Full-scale retaliation is still our best
option!

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:05.439
Even now, while we try to come up with a strategy,
that could be enough to draw him in.

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:08.280
We’re willing him into existence as we speak!”

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.910
“What about deploying another SCP?”

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.520
came a voice from the edge of the group.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.250
It belonged to Junior Researcher Jake Harrison,
a relatively new member of the Foundation,

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.430
who had been reading up on files related to
the Scarlet King.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:25.200
He knew that, in trying to understand and
come up with a way to best the murderous multiversal

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.370
warlord, that he was inadvertently feeding
him power.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:33.310
But Jake seemed to have stumbled on the one
solution that everyone else had overlooked.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:37.489
There was already another anomaly that might
have been perfectly suited for defeating the

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:38.489
Scarlet King…

00:02:38.489 --> 00:02:40.400
“What do you suggest, Harrison?”

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.630
one of the other researchers spat.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.620
“You really think something like SCP-682
would be willing to work with us and destroy

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.760
the Scarlet King?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.760
That’s absurd!”

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.120
“I heard 682 is meant to be one of the Scarlet
King’s children!”

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.120
another remarked.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.060
“No, not 682!”

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:57.879
Jake argued, turning to the researcher that
had just made a comment about the entity’s

00:02:57.879 --> 00:03:02.000
supposed children; a group of anomalies that
were believed to have been born of the Scarlet

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.000
King himself.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.319
“But you’re on the right track.

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:06.860
We use SCP-999.”

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.500
The group of researchers looked dumbfounded
at Jake.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:13.790
He couldn’t tell if they were about to yell
at him, or if they would all burst out laughing.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.239
To his surprise, they actually looked to be
considering his proposal.

00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:22.420
It was widely believed that SCP-999 – the
adorable blob of orange slime known as the

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.420
Tickle Monster – was actually the final
child of the Scarlet King.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.950
“That’s… not entirely implausible,”
one of the researchers answered.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.849
“SCP-999 is believed to be an ultimate force
for good that could, in theory, defeat his

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:37.849
‘father’.”

00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:42.480
“The Scarlet King is meant to be unparalleled
chaos, the two could cancel each other out,”

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.480
another theorized.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:48.879
“But the Tickle Monster – sorry, I mean
SCP-999 – it’s still an infant, a child!”

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:50.000
someone else pointed out.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.090
“Even if it could one day beat the Scarlet
King, it's nowhere near strong enough to yet.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:58.209
We might have days, minutes even, before he
arrives, and I don’t know if 999 has the

00:03:58.209 --> 00:03:59.860
power to stop his father.”

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.650
“Then what if we could make him stronger?”

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.800
Jake replied, a risky idea brewing in his
head.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.160
“Surely you aren’t suggesting…”

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.200
Suddenly, a loud rumbling rang out, like an
earthquake, only much louder.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.669
And instead of coming from the ground below,
the noise was coming from the sky.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:21.320
The Foundation’s researchers raced to the
nearest window, or ran out of the buildings

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.850
they were in to turn their gazes upwards.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:31.039
Scored across the sky above was a deep, blood-red
crack, a wound in the fabric of reality itself.

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:35.840
It was huge, almost covering one horizon to
the next, and everyone looking at it knew

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.130
what it meant.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.419
That crack in the sky heralded the approach
of the Scarlet King.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.550
Junior Researcher Harrison spent the next
hour impatiently trying to get hold of someone,

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.789
anyone who could approve his proposal.

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:52.300
The O5 Council were already swamped with suggestions
for how to stop the Scarlet King, each one

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.449
contributing to his rapid approach.

00:04:54.449 --> 00:04:58.370
Eventually, Jake made it through and spoke
directly with a representative, an underling

00:04:58.370 --> 00:04:59.570
for the O5 Council.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.210
“Listen to me,” he urged.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.590
“I know this isn’t your department, but
I need someone to sign off on this.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:07.590
Please, the lives of everyone in this reality
could depend on it.”

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.250
“What are you proposing?”

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.509
“The Clockworks, SCP-914,” Jake answered.

00:05:12.509 --> 00:05:17.460
“We place SCP-999 inside, speed up the process,
and make him strong enough to stop the Scarlet

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.460
King.”

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:22.759
It was an astronomical gamble, using the anomalous
improvement machine.

00:05:22.759 --> 00:05:29.979
Constructed of a multitude of clockwork components
– cogs, gyros, gears – SCP-914 was a device

00:05:29.979 --> 00:05:36.009
that could be used to enhance or ‘refine’
any object placed inside its ‘Input’ booth.

00:05:36.009 --> 00:05:41.580
Depending on the setting, items could be transformed,
destroyed or vastly improved using the Clockworks.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.979
‘Rough’ setting disintegrated any test
subject, while ‘Coarse’ dismantled it

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:47.660
to its base components.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.120
‘1:1’ replaced any item with an almost
identical copy.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.810
Then, there were the ‘Fine’ and ‘Very
Fine’ settings, the former would cause SCP-914

00:05:55.810 --> 00:06:00.590
to improving any item and the latter capable
of the same but with one key difference.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:06.550
‘Very Fine’ would refine an object even
more, usually by giving it anomalous properties.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:11.699
Jake had read up on SCP-914, and knew that
the Foundation had permitted researchers to

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:13.870
conduct tests using the machine.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:20.250
However, following a catastrophic test, nothing
organic could be tested in SCP-914.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.800
That was a strict rule, no biological organism
or living thing of any description was to

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.840
be placed within the Clockworks.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:32.080
It was Jake’s hope, however, that desperate
times called for desperate measures.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.400
Surely, with the Scarlet King almost upon
them, the Council would waive the restriction

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.500
and allow SCP-999 to undergo refinement.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:44.440
The O5 Council representative’s voice cut
out after Jake made his suggestion.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:49.150
There was a long pause, even without the pressure
of incoming calamity, the silence seemed to

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.770
extend for a painfully long time.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:56.509
Suddenly, someone else spoke up in their place,
a modulated, distorted voice.

00:06:56.509 --> 00:07:01.389
It quickly became clear to Jake he was talking
directly to a member of the O5 Council.

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:05.099
Under a different set of circumstances, he
might have felt honored, but right now it

00:07:05.099 --> 00:07:08.919
was almost as scary as the threat of destruction
by the Scarlet King.

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:13.289
“Listen closely, Junior Researcher,” the
council member said on the other end of the

00:07:13.289 --> 00:07:14.289
comm line.

00:07:14.289 --> 00:07:20.250
“You may think you understand SCP-914, you
may even think that it might aid us in stopping

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.810
the current crisis.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.180
But you are far, far mistaken.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:29.009
You will cease this course of action immediately;
your proposal has been denied.”

00:07:29.009 --> 00:07:30.009
“But wait!”

00:07:30.009 --> 00:07:31.009
Jake protested.

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:32.320
“Surely it could work!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.819
I know biological material isn’t permitted
inside the Clockworks, but that doesn’t

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:37.919
mean it can’t affect living matter.

00:07:37.919 --> 00:07:40.449
SCP-999 is a living organism.

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:44.650
If he really is everything that we think he
is, and if we just put him through the refinement

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:48.050
process, he could-”
“No, Researcher Harrison!”

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.050
the voice barked.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:52.129
“Using the Clockworks would mean we risk
losing SCP-999.”

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:54.250
“What are you talking about?”

00:07:54.250 --> 00:08:00.460
“You appear to have a fundamental misunderstanding
of SCP-914, Junior Researcher,” the council

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.460
member chastised.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:07.610
“It doesn’t merely improve upon existing
objects, but replaces them with a new version

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.050
it creates.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:15.330
If we were to place SCP-999 inside, the creature
as we know it would be gone forever, and – if

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:20.440
it really is capable of stopping this catastrophe
– we will then have lost our ultimate weapon

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.210
against the Scarlet King.”

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.020
“But, but-” Jake tried to say.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.020
“Enough!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.419
Every second we waste discussing our options,
the more power the Scarlet King is able to

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:30.419
amass.”

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:33.250
“So why don’t we stop talking about it
and actually do something!”

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.950
the young researcher shouted, giving in to
his frustration and losing his temper.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.630
The comm line went dead, there was no one
on the other end anymore.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:44.760
Another rumbling sound rippled through the
building, even louder than the last tremor.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.590
Jake ran towards a nearby window and looked
out in horror: it was already too late.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:54.670
The red crack above had split open wider,
and like a tidal wave, hordes of nightmarish

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:58.250
creatures came spilling out, raining down
on the world.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:03.240
At commanding them, sending forth his minions
in a flood of destruction, was the Scarlet

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:04.870
King himself.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.680
Jake was done waiting for permission from
the Council.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.760
He sprinted as fast as he could through the
facility, past panicking researchers fleeing

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.310
for their lives, while security officers and
MTF troops abandoned their posts in the futile

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:20.640
hope they could survive the end of this reality
and all others.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:25.720
Jake forced himself not to pay attention:
he needed to find SCP-999.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.250
The playful blob was often free to roam around
the facility, improving the days of anyone

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.250
it encountered.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:36.700
So, all Jake needed to do was find anyone
who seemed happy despite the catastrophe,

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:40.450
and SCP-999 wouldn’t be far away.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:45.720
Outside, the world began to resemble the nightmare
that everyone had experienced the night before.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:50.170
Cities were burning as monstrous abominations
tore through innocent civilians, and ripped

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:55.810
buildings and cars to shreds, reducing every
nearby standing structure to little more than

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:58.760
rubble with frightening speed and ease.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:04.130
The Scarlet King and his armies had been waiting
for this moment for centuries, millennia,

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:10.390
aeons even, and now nothing could stop them
from unfurling pure, indulgent chaos on this

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.550
reality.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:16.130
They had their work cut out for them, subjugating
and destroying the entire multiverse, but

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:19.100
that isn’t to say they weren’t enjoying
it.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:22.910
People across the Earth were being killed
in droves in the name of the Scarlet King.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:27.900
He diverted a significant portion of his forces
to attacking the SCP Foundation itself.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:32.430
While the boots on the ground MTF troops – the
ones that had remained loyal – were usually

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:37.440
a formidable fight, they were no match for
the eldritch armies of the Scarlet King.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.610
The horde began to set free other anomalies
kept locked up in containment, either by accident

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:47.430
when they stormed the Foundation’s facilities,
or intentionally seeking out their cells to

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.730
spring them.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:52.070
Some SCPs tried to stand up to the Scarlet
King and fight back.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:58.000
The likes of the Plague Doctor, The Specter,
and SCP-2800 all tried their best to ward

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.540
off the oncoming attacks of the Scarlet King’s
foot soldiers.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:06.110
They lasted longer than those who decided
instead to run away, turning heel and trying

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:09.610
in vain to escape the destructive reach of
the Scarlet King.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:15.639
Even anomalies like SCP-106, who could escape
to other plains of existence or pocket dimensions,

00:11:15.639 --> 00:11:16.880
weren’t safe.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:23.310
In hiding, they were only prolonging the inevitable:
the Scarlet King would find them all; no corner

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.160
of the multiverse was safe.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:29.389
And, of course, some SCPs thrived in the catastrophe.

00:11:29.389 --> 00:11:34.540
Creatures like SCP-682, the infamous Hard
to Destroy Reptile, found themselves free

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.420
to exact revenge on the Foundation and humanity
at large.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:43.279
Of these, not all the anomalies gave away
their allegiance – 682 in particular was

00:11:43.279 --> 00:11:48.230
too busy killing anything it came into contact
with, whether they were human or a part of

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.030
the Scarlet King’s army.

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:55.330
But other SCPs gladly swore fealty with the
crimson cosmic conqueror, forming alliances

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:59.920
with the entity responsible for setting them
loose and joining the mass of monstrosities

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.670
he had unleashed.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:06.779
And yet, in the midst of all the chaos, the
calamity, and the millions upon millions of

00:12:06.779 --> 00:12:12.310
deaths, one Junior SCP Foundation Researcher
was still searching for the wholesome orange

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:13.310
blob.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:18.940
Jake Harrison had put all his chips on SCP-999,
and eventually tracked the Tickle Monster

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:19.940
down.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.510
The building around him was crumbling, attacks
from the Scarlet King and his minions bombarding

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.690
every second.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:31.130
As Jake ran into the mess hall, his eyes instantly
caught sight of the ball of orange slime,

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.800
cowering under a table.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.839
“Hey, hey!” he whispered, hoping to coax
it out.

00:12:35.839 --> 00:12:37.850
“It’s okay, I know there’s a lot going
on right now.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.750
Hell, it’s the end of the world outside.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.800
But if you come with me, I think we can fix
it together!

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.430
Come on, little guy, what do you say?”

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.470
As if in reply, SCP-999 immediately leaped
up out of its hiding place.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:52.950
Jake caught it in his arms, instantly feeling
a wave of calm wash over him thanks to the

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.310
Tickle Monster’s calming anomalous effect.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:59.420
He tried to stop himself from fully succumbing
to the good vibes that the gelatinous creature

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:04.240
provided, after all, he still had a job to
do, and time was short.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:08.550
The Scarlet King and his invading army might
have seemed, for the most part, to be indulging

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:14.630
in wanton destruction, decimating cities and
Foundation sites, killing humans left, right,

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.630
and center.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:20.589
But Jake figured that, if there was any method
to their madness, then SCP-999 would be at

00:13:20.589 --> 00:13:22.470
the very center of it.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:27.500
Not even the Scarlet King knew for certain
if SCP-999 really was his offspring.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:31.300
Maybe he had heard the rumors and wanted to
reach the Tickle Monster just before it had

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.820
a chance to stop him, if it even could.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:39.769
If the Scarlet King believed, even for a second,
that his supposed son stood a chance at defeating

00:13:39.769 --> 00:13:45.940
him and ending his reign of terror, then he’d
waste no time hunting the orange blob down.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:50.270
His army of nightmarish creatures would comb
every corner of the world until they found

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.300
SCP-999.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.759
Although they might not think to look inside
the Clockworks.

00:13:55.759 --> 00:14:00.610
Placing the smiling, slimy SCP in the Input
booth, Jake fiddled with the controls for

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.610
SCP-914.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:06.399
He’d never performed any experiments using
the machine before, but it was all pretty

00:14:06.399 --> 00:14:09.800
self-explanatory, throwing the dial to ‘Very
Fine’.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:14.070
He gave a moment’s pause, looking at the
adorable anomaly in the machine.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:18.589
The warning from the Council rang in his ears:
if he activated the Clockworks, he’d, in

00:14:18.589 --> 00:14:20.300
effect, be killing SCP-999.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:25.420
Either that, or the Scarlet King would do
it himself when he found the Tickle Monster.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.339
Neither scenario ended well.

00:14:27.339 --> 00:14:32.520
Then, the thundering sounds of the massacre
outside got louder, screams coming from innocent

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:35.850
people who were being caught in the Scarlet
King’s carnage.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:40.370
There was no question about it: if what Jake
was about to do really could stop all this

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:45.050
mayhem, then it was worth replacing SCP-999
to do it.

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.839
With a deep breath, he flipped the switch.

00:14:47.839 --> 00:14:51.540
The clicking and clacking of the Clockworks’
components whirring into life were drowned

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.519
out by the approaching tremors.

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:55.510
Something was coming…

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:59.360
no, he was coming, Jake thought.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:03.899
The very fabric of the building around him
started shaking, brickwork and cement crumbling

00:15:03.899 --> 00:15:09.180
and falling apart as a large hand, fingers
ending in pointed, crimson claws, wrenched

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:11.000
open the roof with ease.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.509
Looking up in horror, Jake saw that the sky
was a dark shade of red.

00:15:15.509 --> 00:15:20.950
Towering over it, a colossal crimson-clad
warrior looked in on the frightened researcher,

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:22.850
horns protruding from its head.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:28.480
Maybe because SCP-999 was still nearby, the
blob was offering him some kind of positive

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.870
mental protection.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:33.709
Otherwise, the mere sight of the gigantic
monstrous being above him would have driven

00:15:33.709 --> 00:15:35.860
Jake and any other mortal mad.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.670
The Scarlet King was upon him.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:44.699
“WHERE IS HE?” came a booming voice that
sounded like hundreds of screams overlaying

00:15:44.699 --> 00:15:45.699
each other.

00:15:45.699 --> 00:15:50.240
The Scarlet King’s gaze seemed to shift
slightly, turning from Jake as he lay helplessly

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:53.180
on the ground, to look at SCP-914.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:57.389
The machine had fully activated, and couldn’t
be stopped now.

00:15:57.389 --> 00:16:02.199
Either through foreknowledge, or some kind
of cosmic sense, the eldritch monstrosity

00:16:02.199 --> 00:16:05.149
seemed to know exactly what the device did.

00:16:05.149 --> 00:16:06.149
“No…

00:16:06.149 --> 00:16:07.149
no!

00:16:07.149 --> 00:16:10.040
WHAT HAVE YOU DONE?”

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.440
the Scarlet King roared.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:15.990
He raised a gargantuan fist, and brought it
straight down through the air towards Jake.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:21.139
He couldn’t run, the Scarlet King was so
vast in size that there was no way the researcher

00:16:21.139 --> 00:16:23.829
would be able to evade the oncoming strike.

00:16:23.829 --> 00:16:28.130
Jake raised his arms in a futile attempt to
protect himself, despite knowing that the

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:32.060
Scarlet King’s fist would likely plunge
through the very surface of the Earth below.

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:36.550
But then again, maybe the junior researcher
just didn’t want to watch.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.790
There was a pause.

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:39.410
The strike never came.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:43.829
It was only when Jake built up the courage
to open his eyes that he saw what had happened.

00:16:43.829 --> 00:16:49.860
A long tendril of orange slime had reached
out of SCP-914, forming a protective barrier

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.180
between Jake at the Scarlet King.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:57.860
Suddenly, with all the force of a tidal wave,
the newly refined SCP-999 came pouring out

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.110
of the Clockworks.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:03.670
The Tickle Monster’s mass had increased,
he was thousands, if not millions of times

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:04.670
bigger.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.939
Swept aside and out of harm's way by the orange
slime, the junior researcher looked up in

00:17:08.939 --> 00:17:16.470
amazement as SCP-999 reached up into the sky,
able to look its supposed father face to face.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:22.089
The Scarlet King recoiled in horror as the
Tickle Monster engulfed him, pulling the cosmic,

00:17:22.089 --> 00:17:24.230
crimson plunderer into an embrace.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:28.039
As they hugged, there seemed to be a change
in the Scarlet King.

00:17:28.039 --> 00:17:33.480
The eldritch monster had spent all his time,
since the dawn of creation, as a cruel, nihilistic

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.480
conqueror.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:39.919
He had killed and enslaved, devoured ancient
gods, and slaughtered entire planes of existence

00:17:39.919 --> 00:17:41.960
in his quest to annihilate everything.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:46.250
But now, held tight by his gelatinous son,
his heart shifted.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:51.179
It was as if the Scarlet King’s eyes had
been opened, and he could see the beauty of

00:17:51.179 --> 00:17:52.179
creation.

00:17:52.179 --> 00:17:59.220
The sheer, overwhelming goodness of SCP-999,
enhanced by SCP-914, undid the evil of the

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.460
Scarlet King himself.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.150
Only it didn’t stop.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:07.720
As the orange slime engulfed the Scarlet King
in a hug, he began to be unmade.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.850
The Tickle Monster, without even trying to
harm its father, had been made into such a

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:17.870
beacon of pure positivity by the Clockworks
that the Scarlet King simply ceased to exist.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.630
He was unwoven, not killed but rendered without
any purpose.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:27.640
He barely even felt any pain, but at the same
time, was removed from this and every other

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.800
universe.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.740
And still, it didn’t stop.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:35.730
The newly recreated SCP-999 spread across
the world like an orange flood.

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:40.490
The Scarlet King’s armies, the other SCPs,
even the few surviving human beings were all

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:46.880
wiped away, SCP-999 spread to every corner
of the Earth, turning the blue planet orange

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:50.860
as he coated it, purging every single scrap
of negativity.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:57.510
All hatred, all cruelty, all evil – even
that of the SCP Foundation itself.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:02.830
The entire world was unmade by the Tickle
Monster, not out of malice, but so that nobody

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:06.220
anywhere could cause the Scarlet King to remerge.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:11.750
At the same time, all that was left was a
planet-sized ball of orange slime, lonelily

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.160
spinning through space.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:18.970
Now go and check out “SCP-999 THE TICKLE
MONSTER” for more information on everyone’s

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:25.290
favourite orange blob of wholesomeness or
“CHILDREN OF SCP-001 THE SCARLET KING – IS

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:30.039
SCP-999 REALLY HIS SON?”, and explore their
bizarre family tree.

